    gameplay: 'Deal cards to the players and use the stop-card layout defined by the table. Players play cards in suit sequence when possible, with certain cards acting as stops that interrupt the run. Payments or counters are awarded according to the traditional stops and successful runs.',
    keyRules: [
      'Comet belongs to the stops family: play proceeds in ordered card sequences until blocked by a stop.',
      'Key cards and layout spaces carry stake or counter value.',
      'The hand rewards timing: holding a stop can prevent opponents from continuing a sequence.',
